cff-version: 1.2.0
title: PathWeave
message: >-
  PathWeave is a 2D multi-agent pathfinding research and simulation platform.
  It builds on the open-source PyMAPF library; the original library and its
  authors are cited below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mohammad
    given-names: Shoaib
  - family-names: Chowrasia
    given-names: Saurabh
  - family-names: Saha
    given-names: Manav
repository-code: "https://github.com/Shoaib9124/Multi-Agent-PathFinding"
abstract: >-
  PathWeave compares prioritized planning with Space-Time A*, Conflict-Based
  Search and a learned MAPPO policy on identical 2D grid instances. It includes
  an interactive editor, synchronized playback, formal solution validation and
  reproducible batch experiments with CSV export.
license: MIT
version: 0.9.0
keywords:
  - multi-agent pathfinding
  - motion planning
  - conflict-based search
  - prioritized planning
  - reinforcement learning
references:
